# Normalise text to LF in the repository and check it out as LF everywhere.
#
# Why this exists: Python's open(path, "w") on Windows translates "\n" to
# "\r\n", so any file rewritten by a script in experiments/ came back as CRLF
# and produced a whole-file diff instead of a reviewable one. That churn once
# rewrote the frozen First Review dump, which is cited by hash in RESULTS.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXCEPTION -- the frozen Gate A dump.
#
# fever_run_200_gateA.csv is the per-example dump for the construction exactly
# as submitted at First Review. Its committed bytes are fully CRLF (201 CRLF,
# 0 bare LF) because it was produced by the original Windows run, and RESULTS.md
# cites its SHA-256 (70a3a783...84c6b7) as the evidence that it is retained
# unmodified -- the retraction of the 0.745 headline rests on it.
#
# "-text" disables newline conversion entirely, so git stores and checks out
# the bytes verbatim. Without this line the rule above would renormalise the
# file to LF and invalidate the published hash. Do not remove it, and do not
# "fix" the line endings of this file.
fever_run_200_gateA.csv -text

# Binary artefacts, declared rather than left to auto-detection.
*.png binary
